OpenLineage Evaluation – Engineering Notes

Overview

Open source framework for data lineage collection and standardization.

Provides a common language (spec) for lineage events across tools.

Architecture

Core: event-based model (JSON schema).

Collector agents send lineage events → backend (e.g., Marquez).

Marquez = reference implementation providing storage + API + UI.

Integration with Data Sources & Metadata Tools

Native integrations: Apache Airflow, Spark, dbt, Flink, SQL.

Growing connectors ecosystem (community driven).

Metadata integration via Marquez (REST API).

Granularity of Lineage

Supports job → dataset lineage (table/file level).

Column-level lineage supported via dbt and some Spark connectors.

Not yet uniform across all integrations.

Automation of Lineage

Automated: connectors emit lineage during job execution.

Semi-automated/manual: custom emitters can be built with the API.

Visualization of Data Flows

Marquez UI provides lineage DAGs and dataset/job dependency views.

Focus on technical lineage; business context requires add-ons.

Impact & Root Cause Analysis

Backward/forward traversal supported in UI.

Enables root cause analysis by following dependencies.

Enrichment & Contextualization

Mainly technical lineage.

Limited business glossary / data quality features out of the box.

Could integrate with external metadata mgmt platforms for enrichment.

Extensibility

Open API (REST + JSON schema).

Easy to extend with custom emitters.

Flexible but requires engineering effort.

Usability

Marquez UI: clean but basic.

Good for lineage browsing, but not a full data catalog.

Collaboration Features

OpenLineage itself = spec + events, not collaboration.

Marquez adds team-level browsing, but lacks advanced collab features (comments, annotations).

Scalability & Performance

Proven on large Spark/Airflow deployments.

Performance depends on Marquez backend + DB choice.

Vendor / Community Support

Backed by LF AI & Data Foundation.

Active contributors (Datakin, Microsoft, WeWork).

Healthy GitHub repo + Slack channel.
